NEW = '*STATUS: CLOSED 2026-10-19 -- PROVEN BY TWO COLD RUNS on restaurant_row_001, whose lot places deli_a03: 9338 on Deli Counter 0.234.0 and 9339 on 0.235.0 (4fed8011), each 0 interventions. What would close it is met: the table with tests that fail without it (test_open_floor_rules.py, 11; test_ceiling_holes.py, 9), the library rebuilt, `open_floor_baseline.json` empty, L12 0, and L24\'s one more room the objective vault, which the walker\'s rule of 2026-10-06 keeps breach-only. 9338\'s package carried the new kitchen door (`b0 int_0_6_open0`) and the stockroom gate 0.5 m west, and its frames showed what the plans could not: the kitchen wall at x 7 ran under the delis\' 2.2 m drop at (8, -4), its top 0.275 m into the hole and its new door under it -- in all six delis, and in nothing else the table made (`docs/findings/open_floor_table_260/`, "The first cold run: a wall under the drop"). Deli Counter 0.235.0 (`patches/patch_dc_ceiling_holes.py`): layout_lint L27 names a wall under a hole in its ceiling, and the table slides a hole off a wall it stands -- the hole moves, not the wall -- so the six drops moved 0.5 m east into the kitchen and three delis refurnished; the suite 1,618 passed, 2 skipped. 9339: 0 interventions, the pick seed 9003 PASS 90 and findings 81 / 110 as on 9338; the drop\'s nav link moved with the hole (x -43.0 -> -42.5, landing in the kitchen); the 7 drop-edge rows 9338 lost came back as declared drop edges (13 -> 20, 0 undeclared); `interactives.json` identical; the hole from the kitchen and from above, beside 9338\'s, in `docs/cold_runs/cold_9339/hole_9338_vs_9339.jpg`. Left for the walker, each a taste call one table row reverses: the three rows the stairs decided OPEN (`plans/plans.html` in the finding). L27\'s other findings, older than the table, are roadmap 264. Earlier status kept: NARROWED 2026-10-19 -- BUILT: Deli Counter 0.234.0 (a6cbc045, `patches/patch_dc_open_floor_table.py`). `open_floor_rules.RULES` holds one row per pair of room ids -- 20 pairs, not the 17 this item\'s body counts, which grouped the forecourt, cold-room and deck pairs too loosely -- applied to the library by `migrate_open_floor_rules.py` (23 specs) and to every spec `presets.make` writes. Three rows are OPEN where the walker\'s default was WALL, each because a stair stands on the line, the factory\'s call: the office\'s lobby and bullpen (`office_stair_0` at (0, 0)) and corner_deli_heist_01\'s stair well against its two cold rooms (`main_stack`\'s reservation, L21; `cold_n_access`, L18). Found and fixed on the way: the open-floor rule did not count exterior walls (the gas stations\' seven forecourt pairs met their shops along the front wall), and `spec_loader` refused any room naming `open_to`, which the schema had admitted since 0.223.0. A WALL row slides an opening its new wall\'s end would split (the six delis\' stockroom gates, 0.5 m west, L18\'s own prescription) and is taken back whole if it would leave a spec failing a lint rule it passed. The library: 0 open floors nobody named in 159 built specs; L12 0; L24 one room more, rowhouse_raid\'s vault, the objective, kept by the walker\'s rule; tactical graph edges 1,362 -> 1,358, the four lost each crossing a wall with no door; no new lint FAIL; the suite 1,609 passed, 2 skipped; `check.py` passed; the rebuild moved the 23 specs\' records and no others. Plans before and after: `docs/findings/open_floor_table_260/plans/plans.html`. What is left: a cold run on a level whose lot holds one of the 23, and the walker\'s eye on the three rows the stairs decided. Earlier status kept: OPEN 2026-10-19 -- THE WALKER\'S GO: "go ahead with the 255 table, your defaults are good". Not started.*'
ITEM_264 = "\n*STATUS: OPEN 2026-10-19 -- named by layout_lint L27 (Deli Counter 0.235.0); not started.*\n\n**264. Walls under a hole that the open-floor table did not make.** L27 (a wall under a hole in its own ceiling, advisory) names three on the 159 built specs of Deli Counter 0.235.0, each standing there before roadmap 260's table: final_stand's ground-floor wall at y -3 under its atrium (0.30 m into the hole, along 10 m), cbp_town_finale_midbalanced_schemafixed's at y 10 (0.30 m, 28 m), and bank's at x 4, its centreline on its atrium's edge (0.15 m, 6 m). The first two show their whole top as a strip across the void; bank's shows half its thickness at the rim. Among Level Factory's transients it names one more, `presets.casino_tower`'s count-room skylight: a 1.4 m breachable hatch at (14, 8) in storey 1's floor, centred on the storey-0 wall at y 8 between the gaming floor and the cashier cage -- ten category5_baie_dore_001 shells of 2026-09-13, and every casino the preset makes. Measured in `docs/findings/open_floor_table_260/` (`l27.py`, `l27_0235.out.txt`). The rule is the table's -- the hole moves, not the wall, L21's rule for a stair -- but which room a hole should open into is a design question the table answered for its own walls only: the atriums' walls run the length of their voids, and the skylight could drop into the cage or onto the gaming floor. **What would close it:** each named wall clear of its hole by the factory's call, written down where the walker can reverse it; L27 silent on the library and on a fresh casino_tower; the shells rebuilt.\n"
TAIL = ' `light_check` station reported beside the floor it stands on -- dynamic against static as the no-probe control, the sun on and off -- then probes laid at doors, windows, stairs and objectives against the automatic ones, priced with four crew and enemies, and a GI rule handed to the gameplay layer.\n'


def main():
    raw = ROADMAP.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in raw:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: the roadmap has CRLF lines; nothing written")
    text = raw.decode("utf-8")
    if text.count(OLD) != 1:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: roadmap 260's NARROWED status is there %d times, not once; nothing written"
                         % text.count(OLD))
    if "**264. " in text:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: an item 264 is already there; nothing written")
    if not text.endswith(TAIL):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: the roadmap does not end on item 263's last line; nothing written")
    ROADMAP.write_bytes((text.replace(OLD, NEW) + ITEM_264).encode("utf-8"))
    print("roadmap 260 CLOSED, 264 opened; now tools/roadmap_status.py --write and --check")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
